pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: `GeneralPBConstraint::add` (in-situ branch, i64) checked that the
% *unadjusted* degree sum fits into i64 and then subtracted the merge cancellation from it
% with a plain `-`. Here the degree sum is i64::MIN + 2 and merging `5 x1` with `5 ~x1`
% cancels 5, so the true degree is i64::MIN - 3: it used to wrap to a huge positive number
% and turned the trivially true sum into the empty contradiction. The formula is
% satisfiable (x1 true, x2 false).
f 1 ;
pol 1 9223372036854775807 - ;
pol 2 ~x1 5 * + ;
pol 3 x2 w ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 4 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
